From 318dd177bd2587c0d804028cca04921f3785a0ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1aeo <github@1aeo.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 08:43:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/20] relay_metrics: Count tunneled directory requests and
 responses

tor_relay_streams_total{type="BEGIN_DIR"} counts BEGIN_DIR streams, but
nothing after that: whether a stream ever sent a usable request, whether
it asked for an ordinary directory document or an onion service
descriptor, and whether the response left the directory connection.

Add tor_relay_begindir_request_total{type="non_hs|unparsed"} for
tunneled requests that aren't onion service descriptor fetches or
uploads (those are in tor_relay_hsdir_fetch_total and
tor_relay_hsdir_upload_total), with "unparsed" covering a
parse_http_url() failure and a connection closed while waiting for its
request. Add tor_relay_begindir_response_total{type="hs_descriptor|
other"} for responses fully handed to their stream in
connection_dir_finished_flushing(), which does not mean the client
received them.

Only tunneled (BEGIN_DIR) connections are counted, so on a public relay
a BEGIN_DIR stream lands in exactly one of these request types or the
onion service families, or is still waiting for its request. The
counters live in the relay module, with stubs for the dircommon callers.

Part of #41339.
